<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Earned Income Credit Information</title>
    <style>
        @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
        .page {
            width: 794px; height: 1123px;
            padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
            overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
            position: relative;
            font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
        }
        .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
        h1, h2, h3 { font-weight: bold; }
        .section-header { margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
        .two-column { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }
        .column { width: 48%; }
        .caution { border: 1px solid #000; padding: 10px; margin-top: 15px; background-color: #f0f0f0; }
        .tip { border: 1px solid #000; padding: 10px; margin-top: 15px; background-color: #e0ffe0; }
        table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 10px; }
        td { padding: 5px; border: 1px solid #ccc; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="page">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
            <div>
                <h1 style="font-size: 24pt;">SCHEDULE EIC</h1>
                <p style="font-size: 10pt;">(Form 1040A or 1040)</p>
            </div>
            <div style="text-align: right;">
                <div style="font-size: 10pt;">OMB No. 1545-0076</div>
                <div style="font-size: 10pt;">1040A</div>
                <div style="font-size: 10pt;">EIC</div>
                <div style="font-size: 10pt;">Attachment</div>
                <div style="font-size: 10pt;">Sequence No. <span data-field="sequence_number">{{ sequence_number }}</span></div>
                <div style="font-size: 10pt;">Your social security number</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="section-header" style="margin-top: 30px;">Earned Income Credit Information</h2>
        <p style="font-size: 12pt;">Qualifying Child Information</p>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Complete and attach to Form 1040A or 1040 only if you have a qualifying child.</p>

        <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
            <div style="font-weight: bold;">Before you begin:</div>
            <div class="caution">
                <p style="margin: 0;">&bull; See the instructions for Form 1040A, lines 40a and 40b, or Form 1040, lines 66a and 66b, to make sure that (a) you can take the EIC, and (b) you have a qualifying child.</p>
                <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">&bull; If you take the EIC even though you are not eligible, you may not be allowed to take the credit for up to 10 years. See back of schedule for details.</p>
                <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">&bull; It will take us longer to process your return and issue your refund if you do not fill in all lines that apply for each qualifying child.</p>
                <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">&bull; Be sure to check the child's name on line 1 and social security number (SSN) on line 2 agree with the child's social security card. Otherwise, at the time we process your return, we may reduce or disallow your EIC. If the name or SSN on the child's social security card is not correct, call the Social Security Administration at 1-800-772-1213.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="section-header">Qualifying Child Information</h3>

        <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
            <table style="width: 100%;">
                <tr>
                    <td style="width: 30%;">1 Child's name</td>
                    <td style="width: 35%;">First name</td>
                    <td style="width: 35%;">Last name</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td style="width: 30%;">2 Child's SSN</td>
                    <td colspan="2" style="text-align: center;"></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td style="width: 30%;">3 Child's year of birth</td>
                    <td style="width: 35%;"></td>
                    <td style="width: 35%;"></td>
                </tr>
            </table>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">If you have more than two qualifying children, you only have to list two to get the maximum credit.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
            <h3 class="section-header">4 If the child was born before 1988—</h3>
            <table style="width: 100%;">
                <tr>
                    <td style="width: 20%;">a Was the child under age 24 at the end of 2006 and a student?</td>
                    <td style="width: 15%; text-align: center;">Yes.</td>
                    <td style="width: 15%; text-align: center;">No.</td>
                    <td style="width: 15%; text-align: center;">Yes.</td>
                    <td style="width: 15%; text-align: center;">No.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td style="width: 20%;"></td>
                    <td style="width: 15%; text-align: center;"><span data-field="response_a1">{{ response_a1 }}</span></td>
                    <td style="width: 15%; text-align: center;"><span data-field="response_a2">{{ response_a2 }}</span></td>
                    <td style="width: 15%; text-align: center;"><span data-field="response_a3">{{ response_a3 }}</span></td>
                    <td style="width: 15%; text-align: center;"><span data-field="response_a4">{{ response_a4 }}</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td style="width: 20%;">b Was the child permanently and totally disabled during any part of 2006?</td>
                    <td style="width: 15%; text-align: center;"><span data-field="response_b1">{{ response_b1 }}</span></td>
                    <td style="width: 15%; text-align: center;"><span data-field="response_b2">{{ response_b2 }}</span></td>
                    <td style="width: 15%; text-align: center;"><span data-field="response_b3">{{ response_b3 }}</span></td>
                    <td style="width: 15%; text-align: center;"><span data-field="response_b4">{{ response_b4 }}</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td style="width: 20%;"></td>
                    <td style="width: 15%; text-align: center;"><span data-field="response_b1_action">{{ response_b1_action }}</span></td>
                    <td style="width: 15%; text-align: center;"><span data-field="response_b2_action">{{ response_b2_action }}</span></td>
                    <td style="width: 15%; text-align: center;"><span data-field="response_b3_action">{{ response_b3_action }}</span></td>
                    <td style="width: 15%; text-align: center;"><span data-field="response_b4_action">{{ response_b4_action }}</span></td>
                </tr>
            </table>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
            <h3 class="section-header">5 Child's relationship to you</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">(for example, son, daughter, grandchild, niece, nephew, foster child, etc.)</p>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
            <h3 class="section-header">6 Number of months child lived with you in the United States during 2006</h3>
            <table style="width: 100%;">
                <tr>
                    <td style="width: 50%;">
                        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">&bull; If the child lived with you for more than half of 2006 but less than 7 months, enter "7."</p>
                        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">&bull; If the child was born in 2006 and your home was the child's home for the entire time he or she was alive during 2006, enter "12."</p>
                    </td>
                    <td style="width: 50%; text-align: right;">
                        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">months</p>
                        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">months</p>
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td colspan="2" style="padding-top: 10px;">
                        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Do not enter more than 12 months. Do not enter more than 12 months.</p>
                    </td>
                </tr>
            </table>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">You may also be able to take the additional child tax credit if your child (a) was under age 17 at the end of 2006, and (b) is a U.S. citizen or resident alien. For more details, see the instructions for line 41 of Form 1040A or line 68 of Form 1040.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-top: 40px; font-size: 9pt;">
            <p>For Paperwork Reduction Act Notice, see Form 1040A</p>
            <p>Cat. No. 13339M</p>
            <p>Schedule EIC (Form 1040A or 1040) 2006</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <div style="text-align: right; font-size: 10pt;">Page 2</div>

        <h2 class="section-header" style="margin-top: 20px;">Purpose of Schedule</h2>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">After you have figured your earned income credit (EIC), use Schedule EIC to give the IRS information about your qualifying child(ren).</p>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">To figure the amount of your credit or to have the IRS figure it for you, see the instructions for Form 1040A, lines 40a and 40b, or Form 1040, lines 66a and 66b.</p>

        <h2 class="section-header" style="margin-top: 30px;">Qualifying Child</h2>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">A qualifying child for the EIC is a child who is your . . .</p>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Son, daughter, stepchild, foster child, brother, sister, stepbrother, stepsister, or a descendant of any of them (for example, your grandchild, niece, or nephew)</p>

        <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
            <p style="font-weight: bold;">AND</p>
        </div>

        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">was . . .</p>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Under age 19 at the end of 2006</p>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">or</p>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Under age 24 at the end of 2006 and a student</p>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">or</p>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Any age and permanently and totally disabled</p>

        <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
            <p style="font-weight: bold;">AND</p>
        </div>

        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">who . . .</p>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Lived with you in the United States for more than half of 2006. If the child did not live with you for the required time, see Exception to time lived with you beginning on page 42 of the Form 1040A instructions or page 49 of the Form 1040 instructions.</p>

        <div class="caution" style="margin-top: 20px;">
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">If the child was married or meets the conditions to be a qualifying child of another person (other than your spouse if filing a joint return), special rules apply. For details, see page 43 of the Form 1040A instructions or page 49 of the Form 1040 instructions.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-top: 30px; text-align: center;">
            <img src="placeholder_icon.png" alt="Icon" style="width: 30px; height: 30px; vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 10px;">
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Do you want part of the EIC added to your take-home pay in 2007? To see if you qualify, get Form W-5 from your employer, call the IRS at 1-800-TAX-FORM (1-800-829-3676), or go to www.irs.gov.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>